+/// Register the contact material callback, which may override the friction, restitution, rolling
+/// resistance and tangent velocity of each touching contact before the solver runs. This is
+/// optional. Pass NULL to remove it. Every contact then updates on its next step instead of being
+/// recycled, so the new callback reaches contacts that are already resting.
+/// @see b3ContactMaterialFcn
+B3_API void b3World_SetContactMaterialCallback( b3WorldId worldId, b3ContactMaterialFcn* fcn, void* context );
+
+/// Make every contact in the world update on its next step instead of being recycled, so the
+/// contact material callback runs on it again. Call this when the callback's answers change: a
+/// resting contact is recycled on every step and would otherwise keep its old material for as long
+/// as it rests. A contact of a sleeping body updates when the body wakes; this wakes nothing.
+B3_API void b3World_InvalidateContactMaterials( b3WorldId worldId );
